
		QLiberated programs and the Qx0


A - What and why
B - Starting QLiberated programs with the QEXEC (_w) commands
C - Patching QLiberated programs permanently
D - Not Qlib specific
E - COPYBACK always on


A - What and why
=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-
SMSQE 3.42 contains a new scheduler mechanism for the Qx0 machines, so that
QLiberated programs run correctly on that platform even if the machine is in
COPYBACK mode.

For this, SMSQE contains 4 new keywords QEXEC and QEX, QEXEC_W and QEW (note
that QEX and QEW are just shortened versions of the QEXEC and QEXEC_W keywords,
they add no additional facilities.)

QLiberated program must be started with one of these commands.


B - Starting QLiberated programs with the QEXEC (_w) commands
=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-.=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-

The QEXEC etc commands do not modify or patch the code of the program itself,
they just apply a small patch to a program's exception vector table.

QEXEC and QEX don't suspend the calling job, QEXEC_W and QEW do.

Admittedly, these commands are pretty primitive. They accept only two string
parameters: the filename and a possible command line. The parameters
need not be between parentheses. The separator between parameters doesn't
matter.

Example: QEXEC win1_program ; "command_line"

This executes the program, passing it a possible command line in the usual way.

If you start an (unpatched) QLiberated program with anything else, including
launching it from a file manager, that program will still crash as usual on a
Qx0 running in COPYBACK mode.
    

C - Patching QLiberated programs permanently
=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-

The above commands are there to allow for an occasional use of a QLiberated
program. If you routinely use a QLiberated program, you should PATCH this
program. Once patched, it may be started with any of the usual EXEC, EW etc
commands.

There is a ready-made program allowing you to apply a patch to any program.
That program and the patch itself, however, are not part of SMSQE. They can be
downloaded from my site at
	www.wlenerz.com/qlstuff
under the misc utilities section (Qx0_patch).

That is a zip file containing the patch, the patching program and documentation.


D - Not Qlib specific
=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=
The QEXEC commands are NOT specific to QLiberated programs, potentially any
other program that would crash when the Qx0 is in COPYBACK mode, but run
normally when in WRITETHROUGH mode, may be started with these commands



The QEXEC etc commands do NOT modify the QLiberated program in such a way that
the program could run in COPYBACK mode.
Rather, whenever a QEXEC'd program gets a slice of CPU time by the scheduler,
the CPU is put in WRITETHROUGH mode and then put back into COPYBACK mode when
another program gets its time slice...
This means that a patched program will NOT run at the full COPYBACK speed.


E - COPYBACK always on
=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-
As a result of this new policy, Qx0 machines now always run in COPYBACK mode.
The different keywords (SERIALIZD, WRITETHROUGH, COPYBACK) still exist for
compatibility reasons, but they have no effect any more.


